/T (The lectures discuss forty traits that make others dislike us and their opposites that make people like us. Examples include egotism, aggression, pessimism, fault-finding, gossiping, false promises, moodiness and favouritism, set against selflessness, optimism, giving credit, politeness, trustworthiness, honesty and humility. These qualities influence how people perceive us and how successfully we build relationships. Developing good people skills requires understanding others, respecting their opinions and treating everyone fairly.)
