/T (AI-Based Assessment versus Traditional Teacher-Based Assessment in Engineering Education)
/E (AI-Based Assessment versus Traditional Teacher-Based Assessment in Engineering Education)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
733 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Assessment decides how students learn, so the choice between AI-based and teacher-based methods matters in engineering education. Each has clear strengths and weaknesses.)
/E (Assessment decides how students learn, so the choice between AI-based and teacher-based methods matters in engineering education. Each has clear strengths and weaknesses.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
734 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (In terms of accuracy, AI tools are consistent. An automated system can evaluate hundreds of code submissions or objective answers using the same rules every time, without getting tired. Teachers, on the other hand, can understand a student's reasoning in a long derivation or a design report, which software often misses. Therefore, AI is accurate for objective answers, whereas teachers are better for open-ended ones.)
/E (In terms of accuracy, AI tools are consistent. An automated system can evaluate hundreds of code submissions or objective answers using the same rules every time, without getting tired. Teachers, on the other hand, can understand a student's reasoning in a long derivation or a design report, which software often misses. Therefore, AI is accurate for objective answers, whereas teachers are better for open-ended ones.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
735 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Feedback time is where AI wins most clearly. Students receive results and error explanations within seconds, while manual evaluation of a large class may take weeks. Quick feedback lets students correct their mistakes while the topic is still fresh. Conversely, a teacher's comments arrive more slowly but are usually more personal and motivating.)
/E (Feedback time is where AI wins most clearly. Students receive results and error explanations within seconds, while manual evaluation of a large class may take weeks. Quick feedback lets students correct their mistakes while the topic is still fresh. Conversely, a teacher's comments arrive more slowly but are usually more personal and motivating.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
736 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Regarding fairness, AI does not show favouritism or mood-based marking. However, it can carry hidden bias from the data it was trained on, and it may penalise students who give unusual but valid solutions. A teacher can notice such cases and adjust the marks.)
/E (Regarding fairness, AI does not show favouritism or mood-based marking. However, it can carry hidden bias from the data it was trained on, and it may penalise students who give unusual but valid solutions. A teacher can notice such cases and adjust the marks.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
737 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Finally, human judgement remains important. Engineering involves creativity, ethics and teamwork, which cannot)
/E (Finally, human judgement remains important. Engineering involves creativity, ethics and teamwork, which cannot)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
