1030 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 300 0 R
/T (On Bhogi, families clean their homes and throw away old things. On Thai Pongal, they draw colourful kolams at the entrance and cook fresh rice and milk in a new clay pot in the open yard. When the milk boils over, everyone shouts "Pongalo Pongal!" The pot is decorated with turmeric plants and sugarcane. The festive meal includes sakkarai pongal, venn pongal, sambar, vadai and payasam, served on banana leaves. On Mattu Pongal, farmers decorate and worship their cattle, and Kaanum Pongal is a day for family visits and community games.)
/E (On Bhogi, families clean their homes and throw away old things. On Thai Pongal, they draw colourful kolams at the entrance and cook fresh rice and milk in a new clay pot in the open yard. When the milk boils over, everyone shouts "Pongalo Pongal!" The pot is decorated with turmeric plants and sugarcane. The festive meal includes sakkarai pongal, venn pongal, sambar, vadai and payasam, served on banana leaves. On Mattu Pongal, farmers decorate and worship their cattle, and Kaanum Pongal is a day for family visits and community games.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1031 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 300 0 R
/T (Modern eco-friendly practices can preserve the core spirit of the festival. Instead of burning plastic and old tyres on Bhogi, communities can burn only dry leaves or turn them into compost, which reduces smoke and air pollution. Clay pots, banana leaves and areca-leaf plates can replace plastic and thermocol, and kolams can be drawn with natural rice flour. Villages can organise tree-planting drives, rainwater harvesting and cloth-bag campaigns during the festival, and use solar lamps instead of excess electric decorations.)
/E (Modern eco-friendly practices can preserve the core spirit of the festival. Instead of burning plastic and old tyres on Bhogi, communities can burn only dry leaves or turn them into compost, which reduces smoke and air pollution. Clay pots, banana leaves and areca-leaf plates can replace plastic and thermocol, and kolams can be drawn with natural rice flour. Villages can organise tree-planting drives, rainwater harvesting and cloth-bag campaigns during the festival, and use solar lamps instead of excess electric decorations.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
