/T (However, large fairs use a lot of electricity and produce a lot of waste. Modern environmental strategies can solve this. Solar micro-grids, made of rooftop panels and batteries, can power the lights, sound systems and stalls without diesel generators. Zero-waste composting can turn leftover food and leaves into manure for local farms. Organisers can use reusable steel plates, clay cups and cloth banners, provide separate bins for wet and dry waste, and recycle paper and cardboard.)
/E (However, large fairs use a lot of electricity and produce a lot of waste. Modern environmental strategies can solve this. Solar micro-grids, made of rooftop panels and batteries, can power the lights, sound systems and stalls without diesel generators. Zero-waste composting can turn leftover food and leaves into manure for local farms. Organisers can use reusable steel plates, clay cups and cloth banners, provide separate bins for wet and dry waste, and recycle paper and cardboard.)
