/T (On arrival, a site engineer will give a short briefing on how the hybrid plant works. The wind turbines turn on tall towers, and their blades rotate a generator inside the nacelle. We will watch how the strong coastal wind drives them, and how the blades adjust their angle with the wind speed. In the solar section, we will observe rows of photovoltaic panels, inverters and transformers that feed power into the grid. The control room will show how the two sources balance each other: solar power peaks in the afternoon, whereas wind is strong in the evening and night.)
