1192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 305 0 R
/T (Electric vehicles \(EVs\) and internal combustion engine \(ICE\) vehicles are two different answers to the same need, which is transport. Each has clear positives and negatives.)
/E (Electric vehicles \(EVs\) and internal combustion engine \(ICE\) vehicles are two different answers to the same need, which is transport. Each has clear positives and negatives.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 305 0 R
/T (Consider battery life first. An EV battery usually lasts eight to ten years, but replacing it is very expensive. In contrast, an ICE vehicle has no battery problem, though its engine needs regular servicing. As for the manufacturing footprint, EVs create more emissions during production because of battery mining and processing, whereas ICE vehicles have a lighter manufacturing footprint. However, over its lifetime an EV produces far lower emissions, especially when the electricity comes from renewable sources.)
/E (Consider battery life first. An EV battery usually lasts eight to ten years, but replacing it is very expensive. In contrast, an ICE vehicle has no battery problem, though its engine needs regular servicing. As for the manufacturing footprint, EVs create more emissions during production because of battery mining and processing, whereas ICE vehicles have a lighter manufacturing footprint. However, over its lifetime an EV produces far lower emissions, especially when the electricity comes from renewable sources.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 305 0 R
