/Title (Traditionally, a dancer trains for many years under a guru. A performance blends nritta \(pure rhythm\), nritya \(expressive storytelling\) and natya \(drama\), told through hand gestures called mudras, facial expressions and Carnatic music. The dancer wears a bright silk costume, temple jewellery and ankle bells called salangai. The first full solo performance, the arangetram, marks the end of a student's formal training.)
