/Title (On Bhogi, families clean their homes and throw away old things. On Thai Pongal, they draw colourful kolams at the entrance and cook fresh rice and milk in a new clay pot in the open yard. When the milk boils over, everyone shouts "Pongalo Pongal!" The pot is decorated with turmeric plants and sugarcane. The festive meal includes sakkarai pongal, venn pongal, sambar, vadai and payasam, served on banana leaves. On Mattu Pongal, farmers decorate and worship their cattle, and Kaanum Pongal is a day for family visits and community games.)
